# The oracle replays goldens recorded from a POSIX checkout, and a finding's
# snippet carries the fixture's own bytes, so these files have to arrive with
# LF on every platform. `-text` disables end-of-line conversion outright, which
# is also safe for any binary that lands under these trees.
tests/fixtures/** -text
tests/oracle/** -text

# The review bundle embeds CSS as text. Keep its input and generated output
# byte-identical when a Windows checkout would otherwise convert them to CRLF.
ui/component-review/theme.css text eol=lf
crates/context/assets/component-review.js text eol=lf

# Machine-written files that a line diff cannot usefully show. `-diff` makes
# `git diff`, `git show` and `git log -p` print "Binary files differ" instead
# of the content; `linguist-generated` collapses them in GitHub's PR view.
# The in-page bundle carries the wasm module as one ~2.7 MB line, and each
# golden is a JSON object whose captured output is one escaped string, so a
# one-character change rewrites the whole file in a diff. AGENTS.md
# ("Reviewing a PR") has the commands for reading these changes on purpose;
# `git diff --text` restores the raw diff. The bytes, merges and `git diff
# --exit-code` checks are unaffected.
crates/live/assets/detect-antipatterns-browser.js -diff linguist-generated
tests/oracle/golden/** -diff linguist-generated
tests/oracle/vectors/**/*.jsonl -diff linguist-generated

# Written by `cargo xtask bundle` but small and worth reading: collapsed on
# GitHub, kept diffable locally.
crates/live/assets/antipatterns.json linguist-generated

